    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's easy to talk about courage and \"new chapters\" when you're not the one feeling the weight of it all. You talk about a fire that won't die, but I feel nothing but the emptiness. I look at my sword, and for the first time, it doesn't feel like a tool for protection or a symbol of duty. It just looks like an end. A way to finally make the silence permanent, so I don't have to keep pretending there's a path left to walk.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
